<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Āsōpus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> ), i, m.
			(nom. Gr. Asopos, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 7,
		315</span></i>; acc. Gr. Asopon, <i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 3, 6,
			33</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσωπός</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river in Bœotia;</i> personified, <i>the father of Ægina</i>, <i>Evadne</i>, <i>and Eubœa</i>, <i>and grandfather of Æacus</i> (v. Asopis
			and Asopiades), <i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 3, 6,
			33</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river in Thessaly</i>, Liv 36,
			22.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>In Phrygia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 29,
				29, § 105</span></i></div>
